`latest-build` was a BOX-ABSOLUTE symlink (`/opt/scratch/nvme/cx-requal/setup/
build-20260812T065133Z` on the requal box), which is unresolvable on every machine except the
one that wrote it and crashed `check-public-boundary.py` on the CI runner with PermissionError.

It is now a REPO-RELATIVE link to `build-20260812T065133Z/`, which resolves.

CORRECTION (2026-09-01, lane/glm5-accrace): PR #75's sweep replaced the link with a note saying
"the build tree itself was never committed". That is not so — the tree IS committed and always
was, four files deep:

    research/requal-20260812/raw/setup/build-20260812T065133Z/build.log
    research/requal-20260812/raw/setup/build-20260812T065133Z/build.ok
    research/requal-20260812/raw/setup/build-20260812T065133Z/git-status.txt
    research/requal-20260812/raw/setup/build-20260812T065133Z/runtime-binaries.sha256

and its directory basename is exactly the last component the absolute link named. So the fix is
the relative relink, not a note declaring the evidence absent: a receipt note that says raw runs
were never committed, when they were, is how a real receipt gets discarded later by someone
taking the note at its word. The absolute target string is preserved above for provenance.
